# Device-class profile: Jetson Orin (JetPack 5/6, L4T R34+) — GPU-capable node.
# Sourced by deploy/run-node.sh; lives IN THE REPO so new defaults roll out to
# every node via the service's auto-update (no /etc edits per device).
#
# Full-resolution cloud (throughput is point-count-bound; background
# subtraction keeps the subject in budget at 30 fps) + skeleton pose on the
# idle GPU (docs/skeleton_pose.md). The pose flags are SAFE before the
# one-time setup (pip3 install onnxruntime-gpu "numpy<2" + download
# models/movenet.onnx): a missing model/runtime just logs "pose disabled"
# and the node streams normally.
#
# --color-resolution 1536P: capture colour at high res so the renderers that can
# USE it get it. Where it actually adds face-colour DETAIL: depth_to_color (there
# each colour pixel is a streamed point → more res = more coloured points) and
# the future textured mesh (colour decoupled from geometry). In color_to_depth
# (the default/point path) the cloud is DEPTH-grid sized, so colour is capped at
# the depth resolution — a higher source only marginally improves each point's
# single colour (better filtering/registration, and 4:3 covers the depth FOV
# better than 16:9 720p so fewer edge points come out uncoloured). It is free on
# that path (identical point count/RVL/wire; only USB + the SDK warp cost more,
# both cheap on the Orin), so 1536P (2048x1536, 4:3, 30 fps) is a safe capture
# default that pays off the moment you switch to depth_to_color or the mesh.
# --workers 4: headroom for the heavy depth_to_color close-up (one point per
# COLOR pixel ~2.5x the mask/RVL/colour work); the capture->worker-pool->sender
# pipeline overlaps it across the Orin's spare cores (default 2 leaves them
# idle). No effect on the light color_to_depth/subtracted path.
#
# Per-device overrides go in /etc/default/kinect-node EXTRA_ARGS — they are
# appended AFTER these, so a repeated flag there wins (argparse last-wins).
PROFILE_EXTRA_ARGS='--pose-model models/movenet.onnx --pose-trt --color-resolution 1536P --workers 4'
